{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/1390","id":1332090128,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz885PZhUQ","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1390","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1390.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/1390.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/1390","number":1390,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Send peer deltas in MapResponse","user":{"login":"kev-the-dev","id":9502636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk1MDI2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9502636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kev-the-dev","html_url":"https://github.com/kev-the-dev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kev-the-dev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kev-the-dev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kev-the-dev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kev-the-dev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kev-the-dev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kev-the-dev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kev-the-dev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kev-the-dev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kev-the-dev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Summary \r\nImplement the sending of peer list deltas in MapResponse, rather then sending the full list each time. Newer versions of tailscale support this, but it had not yet been implemented in Headscale and was left as a TODO. Sending peer list deltas reduces data usage of the control protocol, especially for larger tailnets. \r\n\r\nThis also fixes a known bug described in #1383, where a peer would not be removed from the network if it is deleted and there are only 2 peers in the network. \r\n\r\nThis is implemented in a way intended to later be expanded to other deltas being sent in MapResponse. It introduces a new struct `mapResponseStreamState` that is forwarded to sequential calls to generate a MapResponse. Over time, this struct can evolve to track more state to move more of the MapResponse to supporting the deltas.\r\n\r\nCloses #1383\r\n\r\n# Testing\r\nThis was tested locally by creating a small tailnet with 2 peers, and deleting one to verify that the other peer is notified of the deleted peer.\r\n\r\nCI unit and integration tests should give reasonable assurance of no other regressions with this change.\r\n","created_at":"2023-04-28T15:55:05Z","updated_at":"2023-09-19T15:20:24Z","closed_at":"2023-09-19T15:20:24Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"261f59c4c88c7d4c58868f07f9efb8043f37e051","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},{"login":"juanfont","id":181059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTA1OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/181059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/juanfont","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont","followers_url":"ht